<spell-notebook "root theming">
	<header level="1">
		Root
		<header>A root loads the components inside it on demand, sets their theme, size, icons and emoji, and shows
              them once they're ready.</>
	</>
	<root-tab-bar showing="theming"/>
	<section>
		<menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
			<item link="#tokens">Tokens</>
			<item link="#themes">Themes</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- THEMING:  no tokens of its own;  what it sets for what's inside. -->
	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			A root has no look of its own, so no `--ui-root-*` tokens. It themes what's INSIDE it:

			- `theme="light"` / `"dark"` sets the colour scheme of everything inside (`:state(light)` / `:state(dark)`).
			- `size` scales the components inside, `mini` ... `massive` (not plain text, nor a bare `<ui-icon>`, which follows its text).
			- Any `--ui-*` token set on the root inherits into every element inside, as on any ancestor.
			- Style the loading look with `::part(loading)` (the loader) and `::part(skeleton)` (the placeholders' box), and
			  a box's scroller with `::part(scroller)`.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```css
			ui-root.dashboard {
			  --ui-primary: var(--ui-teal);
			}
			ui-root.dashboard::part(skeleton) {
			  padding: 1em;
			}
			```
		</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-root" playground>
				<ui-root>
					<ui-segment>
						<ui-header>Report</>
						<p>Every component inside was loaded by the root, on demand.</>
						<ui-button color="primary">Save</>
					</>
				</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>
			Root is ours, not Fomantic's, and draws nothing itself, so no theme restyles it. The site-wide theme (the picker in
			the header) applies to everything inside a root.
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
